<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela oil unions reach deal with PDVSA.</title>
<headline>Venezuela oil unions reach deal with PDVSA.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's main oil union Fedepetrol has reached an agreement with state-owned Petroleos de Venezuela (PDVSA) and the threat of more strikes has been withdrawn, a union boss said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is peace on the shop floor,&quot; said Fedepetrol president Carlos Ortega. &quot;Everything has been resolved.&quot;</p>
<p>Venezuelan unions and PDVSA have been hammering out a deal since Fedepetrol staged an eight-hour strike in February, which met with mixed success.</p>
<p>The talks dragged on for several weeks over performance- related pay.</p>
<p>February's strike had no impact on Venezuela's roughly 2.7 million barrels per day oil exports, but the union had threatened an indefinite strike if no agreement were reached.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Ashby, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2611))</p>
